WEBVTT

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.870
Asukai Kiki...

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:07.700
Born to a family residing in Fukui Prefecture.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:11.160
Rarely attended elementary and middle school.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.040
Expelled from boarding school.

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:15.870
Parents refuse to take her.
Sent to an institution.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.370
Hospitalized at 18 for a suicide attempt.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.830
Leaves the institution and becomes an artist,

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.540
but is repeatedly hospitalized
for three suicide attempts.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.540
Kidnapped by the Challenger at age 21,

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:32.370
and then rescued by Momoki when Narihisago went rogue and shot the Challenger.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:36.040
Despite being hospitalized, she disappears three months later.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.830
Still hasn't been found.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:42.950
The night of her disappearance, a mass
coma incident occurs among the nurses.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.790
Connection is unclear.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:49.660
That's the information that
Director Momoki had stored on the cloud.

00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:54.290
So Momoki was independently
investigating this Asukai Kiki person?

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:55.290
Why?

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:56.250
Who knows.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:01:00.540
For 13 nurses to lose consciousness at once...

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:02.370
What drug could do that?

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.700
I don't know.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.750
Other than the Challenger files
and coma incident news articles,

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.410
everything's gone-- the
school and institution records,

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.330
hospitalization charts, coma incident files.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:15.370
What?!

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:18.870
However, we know exactly who scrubbed it all.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:21.160
If we know who it is...

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:23.080
They're from the Wellside...

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.870
Momoki.

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.290
You got it.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:29.620
Fill the Metropolitan Police in.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:30.870
Yes, ma'am.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.950
Let's continue Hondomachi's rescue operation.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:08.330
Numbers, numbers, numbers.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:10.790
There are countless numbers.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.200
Looks like the lightning will go on forever, too.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.450
The lightning and the numbers.

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:18.660
What could the connection be?

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:22.830
What meaning does this arrangement
of seemingly random numbers hold?

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.410
Does it mean anything at all?

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:29.000
No, it doesn't.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.620
It can't.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:36.290
It's impossible for someone here to
ascertain the sequence the lightning makes.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.000
There are too many numbers.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.700
The strikes are too far away.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:42.870
In other words, to survive in this world,

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:46.410
you don't need to ascertain the sequence!

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.870
Thank goodness.

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:51.410
With so many numbers around...

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.500
This run lasted two minutes 17 seconds.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.750
This is the third run over two minutes.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:00.370
You're lasting longer.

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:03.540
I've been struck over 20 times,

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.910
yet it hasn't gotten any less harrowing.

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.120
We <i>are </i>managing your vitals.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:12.000
Though, to be frank, your
heartbeat's become irregular.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.870
I know you're not actually concerned about my life.

00:04:15.870 --> 00:04:18.950
And of course you don't need to be.

00:04:20.620 --> 00:04:22.500
Did you see the cockpit?

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.330
Yeah.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.410
I see.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.580
It was 89 meters to the cockpit.
Do you think you can make it?

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:30.200
I'm not sure.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.750
Are we gonna continue?

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.410
No, that's not necessary.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:34.790
Oh, really?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:37.450
We have another well for you to dive into.

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:40.450
Ah, of course.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:57.330
The cognition particles weren't on
the body or the outfit, but in the bedroom?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.250
Dammit.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.000
In Director Momoki's id well, sir?

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.370
Yes.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:08.500
Just as Narihisago Akihito's well had a
cockpit, there must be one in his as well.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:12.750
Should that cockpit have
Asukai Kiki's id well loaded,

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.120
you might be able to find Hondomachi there.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:22.000
Further, in order to attempt that, you
need someone to press the eject button.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:26.700
But to have serial killers working together...

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:30.910
Hey, partner!

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:40.660
How does it feel?

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:45.250
To have someone digging
around in your unconscious?

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:48.660
The id well has no effect on my mind.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.370
A stored drive to kill from the past.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:55.500
Certainly it wouldn't contain <i>all </i>of your psyche.

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:58.000
But you of all people must know.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.950
For us serial killers, it could even be called our core.

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:06.830
The kind of thing you could potentially
use to drive a person to suicide.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:08.330
No private conversations.

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:12.160
You can allow a little greeting between colleagues.

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.540
This is Togo.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:18.410
Fukuda, you and Mr. Narihisago
will dive into the same well.

00:06:18.410 --> 00:06:20.580
Why are you a Mr.?

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.660
Does she know you?

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.000
Inside the well, you'll be strangers,

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.330
but do your best to work together.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.410
Okay, but may I say something?

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:30.250
Go ahead.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:34.040
If there are two detectives,
will there be two of Kaeru?

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:36.120
We don't know yet.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.160
This is unprecedented.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.450
But if there's any danger, we'll extract you.

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:42.450
Sure, whatever.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:43.910
One more thing.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:46.330
Tell me, have you ever read a mystery?

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:49.700
--Come again?
--A mystery. A detective story.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:52.040
A few when I was a student.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:55.370
Including classic ones with a brilliant detective?

00:06:55.370 --> 00:06:56.410
Several.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:58.370
That makes things easier.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:03.950
See, normally two brilliant detectives
can't coexist in one mystery novel.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:07.370
If there's only one solution
but two brilliant detectives,

00:07:07.370 --> 00:07:10.330
then one of them has be wrong, right?

00:07:10.330 --> 00:07:14.040
Indeed, the first one would appear
to have revealed the great mystery,

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:18.330
but afterward the second one
would guess at a further layer,

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:21.160
and turn everything on its head.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:25.950
You don't qualify as a brilliant
detective if you get it wrong in the end.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.870
Though, it might barely work if it turns out

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:32.540
the first detective only pretended to get it wrong.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:37.660
My point is, when one of us inevitably loses brilliant detective status,

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.000
will we still be able to remain?

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.290
Alternatively, will the world start to malfunction?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:46.540
We won't get anywhere by debating the issue.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:53.660
Well, whatever problem occurs, you guys
won't be concerned about <i>us </i>anyway.

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:57.450
I do feel like he just presented
a pretty fundamental problem.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:00.580
Injecting Sakaido and Anaido!

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.950
Anaido has opened his eyes.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.410
Though, we aren't receiving information.

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.910
Every aspect of this is untested.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:15.250
Be sure to make observations and records
about what's different from normal, too.

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:17.580
Oh, Sakaido is also waking up.

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:19.500
We have information.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:40.660
Hey there.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.700
You're awake now.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:51.540
Who're you?

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:55.080
Who are <i>you</i>?

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:56.410
What's this?

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:59.450
I don't remember who I am.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:01.830
Oh, so that's what's going on.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:05.370
Then did that girl have amnesia, too?

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:06.910
Girl?

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.660
Hey!

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.290
Kaeru.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.910
Oh, Kaeru.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.410
Sakaido and Anaido have awakened.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:27.620
Has anything malfunctioned so far?

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:28.950
Not that I can tell.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:30.200
I see.

00:09:30.200 --> 00:09:34.160
Then they're both fully in
the world of the same well.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:37.950
As far as the eye can see,
sand, sand, and more sand.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:41.290
Momoki's well is so desolate.

00:09:44.870 --> 00:09:46.540
I've remembered.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:49.120
My name is Sakaido.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:52.290
No full name. Just Sakaido.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.950
The brilliant detective.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:56.330
My name is Anaido.

00:09:56.330 --> 00:09:59.160
Seems I don't have a full name either.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.870
I'm also a brilliant detective.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:03.250
It's a pleasure.

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:04.620
Yeah.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.660
Wow. How cool.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:08.950
I have a job to do.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:10.580
Me, too.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:15.000
Is yours also to solve the
mystery of Kaeru's death?

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.290
In other words, we are here for that purpose.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:24.200
Anyway, Kaeru doesn't
have any external wounds.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:28.750
But she most likely searched for water in the sand.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:31.330
We were buried unconscious in the sand.

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:35.580
But unlike us, Kaeru was conscious and active.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.830
Her activity wore at her stamina,
her dehydration progressed,

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:42.330
and she died of organ damage.

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:45.750
Her cause of death seems to pose no mystery...

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:56.870
Were we wearing watches
or something? They're gone.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:59.500
A watch thief, eh.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:03.290
It might be pretty simple to catch the guy, though.

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:06.410
His footprints are still visible.

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:09.660
Let's go after him. He must know something.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.500
Wait. Let me ask you something first.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.200
Do you have any belongings with you?

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:23.870
Empty-handed.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:26.250
We have neither food nor water.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.500
If we move around in this heat,

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:32.370
before you know it we'll be
dehydrated, and then we might die.

00:11:32.370 --> 00:11:35.040
Wow. That's harsh, but you're exactly right.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.330
Don't point at me.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.870
Basically, Kaeru's body is
here so that we can endure

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:46.000
by drinking the blood and eating the meat?

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:47.830
Don't be stupid.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:48.790
If you drink the blood,

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:54.040
the salt concentration will be so high,
processing it will make you thirstier.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:57.330
Besides, this is not the
time to be eating anything.

00:11:57.330 --> 00:12:00.750
Water is also used in the digestion process.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:02.290
Oh.

00:12:02.290 --> 00:12:04.290
You're a brilliant detective?

00:12:04.290 --> 00:12:05.160
Yep.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.910
Of that much I'm certain.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:08.330
Okay.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.040
Let's just prevent as much water loss as we can.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.160
How?

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.200
Take off your coat.

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:16.250
Oh, that's a good point.
I'm dressed rather warm.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:20.790
No, you need it to protect
your body from direct sunlight.

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:22.330
Then why remove it?

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:24.580
To soak it in urine.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.450
Isn't that a waste of urine?

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:31.580
"Waste"?

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:34.040
Isn't it our only source of water?

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:38.540
If you drink urine, you'll just expend more water.

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:43.620
Water in the bladder doesn't return to
the body, and it's gotta come out anyway.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:45.080
Okay.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.910
What do I do with these now?

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.200
Put 'em on.

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.370
This will prevent some water loss through our skin.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.290
Wrap your coat around your head.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.910
This stinks.

00:13:03.910 --> 00:13:07.700
That takes care of heatstroke
and dehydration for a while.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:11.370
We have other things to think about.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:12.200
Yep.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.790
Okay, let's go catch the watch thief.

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:15.620
Wait.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:18.950
We haven't finished making observations here.

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:22.870
The sand will bury both her body and our footprints in no time,

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.330
so I doubt we can return once we leave.

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:29.790
Then the watch thief's trail will
be buried even faster, won't it.

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:31.540
Shall we split up?

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:34.000
It's best not to act rashly.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:36.580
On top of not knowing the situation at all,

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:39.450
we might not catch up to whoever was here.

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:42.080
The trail might disappear partway,

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:46.750
or we might run out of steam before we catch up.

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:50.000
All these mights.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:51.200
Four of them.

00:13:51.200 --> 00:13:52.620
Don't you mean three?

00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:55.000
If only, right?

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.580
But you see, you said it at the beginning.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:13:59.500
"If we move around in this heat,

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:04.660
before you know it we'll be dehydrated, and then we might die."

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:07.830
Yeah. Still, it's true.

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:10.120
I'm not saying to ignore the footsteps.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:13.000
I'm saying we should prioritize deductions.

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:14.870
Deductions?

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:17.950
Kaeru's cause of death isn't suspicious.

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:21.330
But the watch thief did leave footprints we can follow.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.450
What else is there?

00:14:22.450 --> 00:14:24.000
Just hold on.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:31.910
There are two of us.
Maybe we're <i>supposed </i>to split up.

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:33.120
That must be it.

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:34.410
I'll go ahead.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:39.250
Once you're satisfied with your
observations, you can follow <i>my </i>trail.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:43.040
Finish up before the wind erases it.

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:47.120
What's got him in such a rush?

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:57.330
Don't think that all brilliant detectives are as weird as him, Kaeru.

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:05.000
So far, we haven't seen a single bug.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.040
Also not a single plant.

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:08.660
But there is one thing.

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:12.040
The sun hasn't moved from its apex south of zenith.

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:13.660
Time is stopped.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:17.160
Still, at least Anaido is surviving this time.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:20.660
Hopefully he'll at least reach
whoever left the footprints.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:22.580
Sakaido is moving.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:42.410
Hey. You finally made it.

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:43.910
Are you all right?

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:45.410
I'm great.

00:15:45.410 --> 00:15:49.950
Your legs are wobbling.
You're expending too much energy.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:52.620
Do you think this desert has an exit?

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.120
I expect not.

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:56.160
That was quick.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:58.580
Why do you think that?

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:00.370
The sun isn't moving.

00:16:00.370 --> 00:16:02.620
This place is not normal.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:03.540
Yeah.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:05.660
I wonder how that works.

00:16:05.660 --> 00:16:08.950
Did the speed of Earth's revolution suddenly rise?

00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:11.660
Or did the speed of rotation suddenly fall?

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:13.620
I don't think that's the issue.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:18.000
This place... how do I put it...
feels like it's a desert world.

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:20.330
Like there's nothing but desert.

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:23.410
Well, even if there is a world outside this desert,

00:16:23.410 --> 00:16:26.660
I expect it's utterly impossible for us to reach it.

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:31.120
In other words, what comprises this world is a massive amount of sand,

00:16:31.120 --> 00:16:36.000
Kaeru's body, the watch thief who
might know the mystery of her death,

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:39.250
and of course, us, the brilliant detectives.

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:45.160
Seems like once we solve the case,
this world will lose its raison d'être.

00:16:45.160 --> 00:16:47.120
And him.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:02.080
Which one of us is unsteady on his feet now?

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:05.250
Be quiet. The sand collapsed.

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:09.870
Shit!

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:13.750
That's quicksand.

00:17:13.750 --> 00:17:15.040
Don't panic.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.910
Stop struggling.

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:20.620
If you thrash around, it'll only suck you in faster.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:24.160
Here I thought you were
well-versed in desert survival,

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:27.410
but maybe it was just piss and blood.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:29.620
Shut up.

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:36.000
All hells are the same.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:40.660
The more you struggle to escape
the pit, the stronger its hold becomes.

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.870
Skip the lecture.

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.910
But this is important.

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:48.580
It takes time for hell to
completely swallow someone up.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:52.370
During that time, you can just gradually crawl out.

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:12.040
What do you know?
He really is a brilliant detective.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:13.450
I heard that!

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:15.410
I told you, didn't I?

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:20.370
But you know, to be honest,

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:25.410
I didn't specifically know how to escape quicksand.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:29.080
I just applied the general theory concerning hell.

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.790
I'm glad it worked out.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:31.830
Brother.

00:18:31.830 --> 00:18:33.250
"Brother"?

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.080
You're a strange one.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:41.290
Do you intend to remain silent?

00:18:41.290 --> 00:18:44.500
As a fellow officer, help us out with this.

00:18:44.500 --> 00:18:46.040
We have you.

00:18:46.040 --> 00:18:47.200
No matter.

00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:53.290
Your friends might just deliver
the missing pieces to us for you.

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:58.830
How does it feel to have the people
you once led trying to take you down?

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.330
They're exploring a well?

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:02.910
Yeah, yours.

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:04.370
Mine?

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.830
Stop them!

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:12.620
They need to extract right now!

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:18.450
Are you okay?

00:19:18.450 --> 00:19:19.660
Yep.

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:21.700
Are <i>you </i>okay?

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.950
I could carry you.

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:26.580
As if you were any state to try that.

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:29.370
Doesn't one of us need to last longer?

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:32.040
If we go down at the same time...

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:34.120
Good point. In that case...

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:36.080
I'll die first.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.330
I get the feeling I should.

00:19:38.330 --> 00:19:40.330
Hey, just hold on.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:41.370
I'm serious.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:44.790
No, I'm saying there's no need.

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:46.080
Look.

00:19:53.540 --> 00:19:56.500
The wind didn't do this, did it?

00:19:57.870 --> 00:19:59.500
Certainly not.

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.620
This is quite something!

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:12.370
He made it all this way
just to succumb to quicksand.

00:20:12.370 --> 00:20:14.540
He's one unlucky fellow.

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:18.910
Let's get a look at this watch thief.

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:19.910
Yeah.

00:20:21.620 --> 00:20:23.950
We made it here together.

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:28.290
Good grief. Just dig him up.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.580
This is more macabre than just quicksand.

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:41.700
Run facial reconstruction.

00:20:41.700 --> 00:20:42.830
Roger that.

00:20:43.910 --> 00:20:45.250
Hey.

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:46.450
Look there.

00:20:50.000 --> 00:20:52.040
It was here?

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:56.040
What... is this thing?

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:10.080
Although the quicksand got him...

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:14.540
He led us here. With his footprints in the sand.

00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:16.580
Yeah. Come to think of it,

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:20.290
it's strange to steal a watch in the middle of a desert.

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:23.000
You just realized that?

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:26.790
I thought you said "watch thief" out of convenience.

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.080
What?

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:29.450
Oh well.

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:33.000
Regardless, this machine was waiting for us.

00:21:37.120 --> 00:21:38.870
Look at this.

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:43.660
Asukai Kiki!

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:46.290
I don't know who that is.

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:50.000
And I don't know what this is.

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:55.120
But for now, I guess I'll try this "enter" option.

00:21:55.120 --> 00:21:57.910
After ten minutes, push eject.

00:21:59.410 --> 00:22:02.200
Ten minutes, huh.

00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:04.910
Assuming we live that long.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:08.410
I'll just go solve the mystery.

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:09.750
You're right.

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:12.200
Good luck, brilliant detective.

00:22:12.200 --> 00:22:13.500
Thanks.

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:17.410
We're not extracting them, right, Director?

00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:20.950
It's just temporary. Stick with Assistant Director.

00:22:20.950 --> 00:22:23.790
Yes. Let Sakaido do this.

00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:27.500
It certainly looks like the
Mizuhanome is inviting him,

00:22:27.500 --> 00:22:31.950
and this is why we dispatched two
brilliant detectives in the first place.

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:38.330
If there really is a well within the well,
I hope he can find Hondomachi in it.

00:22:38.330 --> 00:22:43.750
Also, I'd appreciate it if he could
find out more about this Asukai Kiki.

00:22:45.250 --> 00:22:48.790
I get the feeling this is reckless, but here goes.

00:22:48.790 --> 00:22:51.540
Don't worry. This is the answer.

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:55.580
As a brilliant detective, I can tell.

00:22:55.580 --> 00:22:59.830
We were right about everything.

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:05.000
And this was all arranged
so things would turn out this way.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:07.290
They need to extract!

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:09.040
It was all a trap!
